meta {
  name: road-tax
}

docs {
  # Road Tax Journey (ENG-1398)

  A fleet owner (TORG_ADMIN of staging test company 315) reads and enters a truck's road tax, then
  sees it on the fleet compliance list and on the truck detail. Endpoints live in plutus-java
  `TruckResource`: `GET/PUT /api/trucks/{truckId}/road-tax`, `GET /api/trucks/compliance`, and
  `GET /api/trucks/{id}` (`truckDocuments.roadTax`).

  Run requests 1-9 in order (environment "staging"):

  - 1-2: the owner logs in (OTP `776677`). The token is kept in a runtime var
    (`plutusRoadTaxToken`), so nothing is written to the environment file.
  - 3: read the road tax. Before the first run the status is `NOT_AVAILABLE`.
  - 4: PUT a period over one year without `confirmLongPeriod`: refused, message starts
    `CONFIRM_LONG_PERIOD`.
  - 5: PUT without a proof file: refused ("Proof is required").
  - 6: valid QUARTERLY entry, valid from 2026-10-01, so valid up to 2026-12-31 (source `USER`).
    Note: once the date passes 2026-12-31 the status turns EXPIRED, and step 8 then expects it first.
  - 7-9: the saved row shows on the road-tax GET, the compliance list and the truck detail.

  Errors come back with HTTP 200 and the code in the body (`statusCode`, `message`).
  Step 6 writes a road-tax row on staging truck `plutusRoadTaxTruckId`; rerunning overwrites it.
  The proof key is a dummy string; no upload is made.
}
